    "question_html": "<p>A machine depreciates at 20% per annum on reducing balance method. If its original cost was ₹1,00,000 and its ultimate scrap value is ₹30,000, the effective life of the machine is approximately:</p>",
    "options": {
      "A": "4.5 years",
      "B": "5.4 years",
      "C": "6.2 years",
      "D": "7.0 years"
    },
    "correct_option": "B",
    "answer_html": "<p><strong>Answer:</strong> (B) 5.4 years — Scrap Value = P(1 - r)ⁿ ⇒ 30,000 = 1,00,000(1 - 0.20)ⁿ ⇒ 0.3 = (0.8)ⁿ ⇒ n = log(0.3) / log(0.8) ≈ -0.52288 / -0.09691 ≈ 5.395 years ≈ 5.4 years.</p>",
